+We measure the inclusive muon-neutrino charged-current cross section simultaneously in five observables: muon transverse and longitudinal momenta, available hadronic energy, three-momentum transfer and hadronic invariant mass. MINERvA medium-energy open data are unfolded with OmniFold without binning and reported in sixteen cells. The median relative uncertainty per cell is \fvval{sigmed-reported}\%, including a run-period contribution estimated after differences between periods were observed. As a descriptive comparison, three external generator predictions give $\chi^{2}$ values of \fvval{g-ext-chi2int-min16}--\fvval{g-ext-chi2int-max16} for \fvval{g-gcv-total-ndf} degrees of freedom; GiBUU gives \fvval{g-gibuu-total-chi2int} on the \fvval{g-gibuu-ncells-word} cells covered by its sample. The unfolding reproduces the published muon-kinematic cross-section integral within about 1\%, with a correlated shape difference. Fake-data studies find residual bias exceeding uncertainty-based thresholds fixed in advance at a GiBUU-like truth and a synthetic momentum-transfer tilt. The coverage of the reported uncertainty intervals has not been validated.
 \end{abstract}
 
