+The reported covariance of the sixteen-cell result (Sec.~\ref{sec:cov16}) is a sum of blocks, grouped as follows.
+\begin{itemize}
+\item \textit{Statistical}: the bootstrap of the data, \fvval{s1-stat-replicas} replicas.
+\item \textit{Flux}: \fvval{fb-universes} hadron-production (PPFX) flux universes, weighted by the neutrino--electron and inverse-muon-decay constraint (effective number \fvval{s1-flux-neff}).
+\item \textit{Interaction}: the \fvval{s1-n-interaction} interaction-model bands of the MINERvA systematic set, which reweight simulated events.
+\item \textit{Detector}: the \fvval{s1-n-detector} detector-model bands, which reweight simulated events: the MINOS muon-matching efficiency and the GEANT4 neutron, pion and proton reweights.
+\item \textit{Lateral}: the \fvval{s1-n-lateral} bands that shift the reconstructed kinematics of each simulated event rather than reweighting it: the beam angle in two directions, the muon momentum resolution, and the muon energy scales in MINERvA and in MINOS.
+\item \textit{Normalization}: \fvval{sigmed-normalization}\,\% in every cell.
+\item $C_{\mathrm{model}}$, $C_{\mathrm{resp}}$ and $C_{\mathrm{PL,5D}}$, as defined in Sec.~\ref{sec:cov16}.
+\end{itemize}
+The statistical, flux, interaction, detector, lateral and normalization groups, with a training-seed block that is zero in every cell, form $C_{\mathrm{e}}$, and $C_{\mathrm{total}}=C_{\mathrm{e}}+C_{\mathrm{model}}$. Table~\ref{tab:groups16} gives each group's relative uncertainty in each cell, and Table~\ref{tab:corr16} the correlation matrix of the reported covariance. With the cross sections and the marginal uncertainties of Table~\ref{tab:result16}, the correlation matrix gives the reported covariance to the printed precision; the covariance is also provided in the Supplemental Material.
