   \item (e), the joint-test estimator: a deterministic LightGBM variant with the unbinned negative-weight background treatment (App.~\ref{app:negweight}), whose refinement classifier has 400 trees and 31 leaves. The negative-weight treatment reduces the purity method's nominal-truth bias in the highest-$W$ column at least fifteen-fold (from \SIrange{3.5}{4.1}{\percent} to \SIrange{0.11}{0.24}{\percent}, the level of the no-background closure), and the larger refinement classifier removes most of the background-related bias that remains (\S\S\ref{sec:val-negweight}--\ref{sec:val-departure}). It gives the 3D and 4D central values (\S\ref{sec:3d}) and the sixteen-cell five-dimensional result (\S\ref{sec:fived16}). It is used for the generator tests (\S\ref{sec:joint5d}), the study of generator shapes held out of its development (\S\ref{sec:val-departure}) and the precision study (\S\ref{sec:gbdt-model-dependence}). It was selected before the joint-test design was fixed (\S\ref{sec:joint5d});
   \item (b), the exact-split cross-check above.
 \end{itemize}
-Configuration (c) is the deterministic variant with purity-based subtraction, and (d) is the same variant with negative weights and a nominal-capacity refinement; they serve the background-bias, generator-sized-change and coverage studies listed in the table. The five-dimensional central value of \S\ref{sec:eavailw} and its five-axis covariance use configuration~(a): they were produced before the purity bias was found and the refinement was developed. A refined five-dimensional data unfolding (configuration~(e)) gives the sixteen-cell result; its reported covariance on the sixteen cells is described in \S\ref{sec:fived16-cov}. The 2D central value and its covariance were rebuilt with configuration~(f) after a two-dimensional closure test with backgrounds found the purity bias (App.~\ref{sec:negweight-footing}). The exact-split central value was the quoted 2D central value until 2026-10-11; studies labeled \emph{exact-split} use it and have not been recomputed. The 3D and 4D central values have been regenerated with configuration~(e); no 3D or 4D covariance is quoted.
